Z||000000||hutch84fierose||08-09-2001||10:19 PM||||I was wondering how to edit and change fieros and I would like to see any fieros that have been edited anything I think they look awesome.  I foyu don't mind say the program that you used and how you used it thanks jon||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||08-09-2001||11:12 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ponchop1.jpg">  <BR>and<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/finovert.jpg">  <BR>I used a combo of Arcsoft Photostudio 2000 and Adobe Photoshop 5<BR>Photostudio is easier to use for beginners, but you don't get as good of a result (see above) I tried using Photoshop to make them look a little better but it's not too much help. <BR>What i did was:<BR>On the silver Finale, I repositioned the roof, basically turning the front section clockwise and the rear section counterclockwise, which gave it the chopped look I wanted. Then I selected the car and the lower half of the picture then moved it up so that it covered up the hole made by cutting and moving the roof sections.<P>The silver Fino was done by moving the top section of the windshield down so the windshield was smaller, then I covered the rear of the roof up and drew a boot for the convertible top. And did a little painting to make the trunklid.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
